<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#FFFFFF', position: 'relative' }}>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 0, left: 0, width: 1280, height: 64, background: '#1E4FA8', flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', paddingLeft: 44, paddingRight: 44 }}>
    <Text style={{ color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 26, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>Error bars you can defend &mdash; and where you cannot</Text>
    <Text style={{ color: '#C9D9F2', fontSize: 14, marginLeft: 'auto' }}>04 · Results</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 100, left: 60, width: 700, flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Image src="assets/appdomain.png" style={{ width: 700, height: 284 }} />
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15.5, color: '#4A5568', marginTop: 18, lineHeight: 1.5 }}>Error rises monotonically with distance from the training set: RMSE 0.70 at similarity &gt; 0.7 versus &asymp;1.0 below 0.5. The rule that follows: quote a conformal interval only when the nearest-neighbour similarity exceeds 0.6 &mdash; below that, rank a series internally, but keep the interval out of the synthesis decision.</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 100, left: 800, width: 420, flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 19, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1A2230' }}>Conformal coverage (nominal 80% / 90%)</Text>
    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', marginTop: 16, borderBottom: '2px solid #1E4FA8', paddingBottom: 8 }}>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#8B97A8', width: 210 }}>Protocol</Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#8B97A8', width: 100, textAlign: 'right' }}>80%</Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#8B97A8', width: 100, textAlign: 'right' }}>90%</Text>
    </Box>
    {[
      { p: 'Random split (control)', a: '0.79', b: '0.89', hl: false },
      { p: 'Scaffold split, in domain', a: '0.77', b: '0.88', hl: false },
      { p: 'Scaffold split, all', a: '0.73', b: '0.87', hl: false },
      { p: 'Scaffold split, out of domain', a: '0.54', b: '0.77', hl: true },
    ].map((r) => (
      <Box key={r.p} style={{ flexDirection: 'row', paddingTop: 11, paddingBottom: 11, borderBottom: '1px solid #E5E7EB' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 15.5, color: r.hl ? '#D9534F' : '#1A2230', width: 210, fontWeight: r.hl ? 'bold' : 'normal', lineHeight: 1.3 }}>{r.p}</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 15.5, color: r.hl ? '#D9534F' : '#1A2230', width: 100, textAlign: 'right', fontWeight: r.hl ? 'bold' : 'normal' }}>{r.a}</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 15.5, color: r.hl ? '#D9534F' : '#1A2230', width: 100, textAlign: 'right', fontWeight: r.hl ? 'bold' : 'normal' }}>{r.b}</Text>
      </Box>
    ))}
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#4A5568', marginTop: 18, lineHeight: 1.5 }}>Exchangeability holds under random splitting (control matches theory) and fails for out-of-domain compounds &mdash; the interval is optimistic exactly where it matters most.</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 672, left: 60, width: 1160, flexDirection: 'row' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#8B97A8' }}>AIDD8122 Final Project &mdash; Trust Before Throughput</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#8B97A8', marginLeft: 'auto' }}>09 / 15</Text>
  </Box>
</Slide>
